# earlyoom settings for this host (#541) — replaces the package's /etc/default/earlyoom.
# Thresholds stay at the defaults (SIGTERM at <=10% available, SIGKILL at <=5%;
# with no swap, memory alone decides). Only the victim order changes:
#
#   --avoid   the exedev user manager. oom_score_adj 200/100 puts dbus-daemon (800),
#             systemd --user and (sd-pam) (~734) at the top, so on the defaults
#             earlyoom kills them first and frees ~5 MiB each.
#             And tailscaled (#568): `--accept-dns` points /etc/resolv.conf at
#             MagicDNS, so every lookup, the DB host's included, goes through it;
#             at ~672 it is otherwise the first pick.
#   no --prefer since #568. It named Qdrant and Ollama, the heavy restartable
#             consumers, until SocratiCode moved to co-index. Measured 2026-09-29,
#             the order is now systemd-logind (8 MiB), systemd-timesyncd, cron,
#             earlyoom, journald (under 30 MiB together), then the API
#             (oom_score_adj -900): its first kill that frees real memory is
#             production. Nothing heavy and restartable remains to prefer (#588).
#   sessions  never. exe.dev starts them at -1000, and earlyoom 1.7 skips -1000
#             exactly as the kernel does (kill.c:242-253; its -d table prints badness
#             before that skip). Only a launch under `choom -n 500 --` is reachable
#             (#563, skills#331).
#
# systemd word-splits $EARLYOOM_ARGS itself: no spaces, quotes or backslashes inside
# a value (tests/test_infra_host_memory.py). Matched against /proc/<pid>/comm.
# Install: /etc/default/earlyoom + `systemctl restart earlyoom` (docs/COMMANDS.md).
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 3600 --avoid ^(systemd|.sd-pam.|dbus-daemon|tailscaled)$"
